WHAT YOU MAY DO

  * Read, print, download and keep any part of it, for as long as you like.
  * Share it — give a classmate a copy, put it on a college notice board,
    email a unit to a study group, mirror it for offline use.
  * Adapt it — translate it, rewrite an explanation, extract the worked
    examples, build a question bank from it.
  * Use it while teaching, including in a classroom.


WHAT YOU MUST DO

  * Credit NRSTATLAB, and say where you got it. A link back is enough.
  * Say if you changed anything, so a reader knows a passage is yours and
    not this site's.
  * Release anything you build from it under this same licence, so it stays
    as open for the next person as it was for you.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  * Sell it, or anything substantially made from it.
  * Put it behind a paywall, a login, or a paid course.
  * Use it to advertise or promote a paid service.
  * Strip the attribution, or present the material as your own work.

"NonCommercial" is the licence's own term and it is broader than it sounds:
it rules out use primarily intended for commercial advantage or monetary
compensation. If you teach at an institution that charges fees and you are
unsure whether your use qualifies, ask rather than assume — permission for
genuine teaching use is not something this project intends to withhold.


A NOTE ON THE PUBLISHED SITE

This material is served as a static website, which means every page arrives in
a reader's browser as plain HTML and can be saved, printed, or copied. That is
deliberate: the site is free to read, needs no sign-in, and works offline once
saved. This licence is not an attempt to prevent that. It exists so that the
material stays freely available and properly credited, and so that republishing
it for profit is answerable.


CONTACT

